    {
      "id": "write-block-default-value-54e107",
      "name": "WriteBlockDefaultValue",
      "category": "BlockedDenseGrid3",
      "signature": "WriteBlockDefaultValue<FuncType>(Target, Block Index, Func, Deallocate Bock)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "TBlockedDenseGrid3*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Block Index",
          "type": "Int"
        },
        {
          "name": "Func",
          "type": "FuncType"
        },
        {
          "name": "Deallocate Bock",
          "type": "Bool",
          "default": "true"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<FuncType> void",
      "docs": "TBlockedGrid3 represents a 3D uniform grid.\nThe grid is allocated in BlockSize^3 blocks on-demand (BlockSize is a compile-time constant) allowing\nvery large grids to be used without having to pre-allocate all the memory, eg for sparse/narrow-band use cases.\nBlock-level default values are returned when querying a grid cell in an unallocated block.,\nBlock-level access is provided to facilitate parallel algorithms.  Additionally, 'Set' methods are provided that utilize\ncritical sections provided by the caller."
    },
